-- Q3926: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 409A and Rev. Proc. 92-64, a rabbi trust is a grantor trust where assets must remain available to the employer''s general creditors upon insolvency. This creditor exposure is what prevents constructive receipt and defers taxation.
Wrong (A): Rabbi trust assets are not protected from creditors. The lack of creditor protection is the defining feature that enables tax deferral.
Wrong (B): The executive is not taxed when contributions are placed in the trust because the funds remain at risk of forfeiture to creditors.
Wrong (D): There is no requirement that rabbi trusts be funded with government securities. The trust may hold various investment types.$EXPL$
