-- Q3927: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sec. 422(a), ISO favorable treatment requires holding shares at least one year from exercise and two years from grant. Selling 10 months after exercise is a disqualifying disposition under Sec. 421(b). The $15 spread at exercise ($40 - $25) is ordinary income, and the $15 post-exercise gain ($55 - $40) is long-term capital gain because the shares were held over one year from grant.
Wrong (B): The entire $30 gain cannot be long-term capital gain because the one-year holding period from exercise was not met, triggering a disqualifying disposition.
Wrong (C): The post-exercise gain is long-term capital gain (held over one year from grant date), not short-term.
Wrong (D): Only the exercise spread is ordinary income. The post-exercise appreciation is capital gain, not ordinary income.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3927;

