-- Q3930: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 83(a) and Treas. Reg. 1.83-3(e), RSUs are taxed as ordinary income at the fair market value on the vesting date when shares are delivered. A Section 83(b) election is unavailable because no property is transferred at grant.
Wrong (A): RSUs are not taxed at the grant date because no property is transferred at that time. Taxation occurs at vesting when shares are actually delivered.
Wrong (B): RSUs are not tax-free until sale. Ordinary income is recognized at vesting, and only subsequent appreciation is taxed at sale.
Wrong (C): RSU income at vesting is ordinary income, not capital gain. Capital gain treatment applies only to post-vesting appreciation.$EXPL$
