-- Q3931: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 132(b), a no-additional-cost service is excludable if the employer incurs no substantial additional cost (including forgone revenue) and the service is offered in the same line of business where the employee works. Nondiscrimination rules under Sec. 132(j)(1) also apply.
Wrong (B): There is no $100 dollar threshold for no-additional-cost services. The test is whether the employer incurs substantial additional cost, not a specific dollar amount.
Wrong (C): The benefit must be available on substantially similar terms to all employees, not limited to highly compensated employees.
Wrong (D): The employer does not need to charge 50% of retail. The requirement is no substantial additional cost to the employer, not a minimum employee charge.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3931;

-- Q3933: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 404(a)(5), the employer''s deduction for NQDC is deferred until the year the compensation is includible in the employee''s gross income. This matching principle ensures the employer cannot deduct the expense before the employee recognizes the income.
Wrong (A): The employer cannot deduct NQDC in 2026 when earned because the matching rule ties the deduction to the employee''s income inclusion year, not the service year.
Wrong (B): The deferral election year is irrelevant for the deduction. The deduction depends on when the employee actually includes the compensation in income.
Wrong (D): The employer does receive a deduction for NQDC, but it is delayed until the employee recognizes the income under the Sec. 404(a)(5) matching rule.$EXPL$
