  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 132(c), a qualified employee discount on merchandise is excludable up to the employer''s gross profit percentage. Any discount exceeding that percentage is included in the employee''s gross income as compensation.
Wrong (B): The 25% threshold is not the statutory limit. The limit is the employer''s actual gross profit percentage, which varies by employer.
Wrong (C): The 50% figure is not the statutory limit for merchandise discounts. For services, the limit is 20% under Sec. 132(c)(1)(B).
