UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sec. 61(a), both the $75,000 signing bonus and the $10,000 moving expense reimbursement are includable in gross income, totaling $85,000. The TCJA suspended the moving expense exclusion under Sec. 132(a)(6) for non-military taxpayers through 2025, and this suspension has been extended.
Wrong (B): $75,000 omits the moving expense reimbursement, which is also taxable under current law since the Sec. 132(a)(6) exclusion is suspended.
Wrong (C): $10,000 omits the signing bonus. Signing bonuses are taxable compensation under Sec. 61(a).
Wrong (D): Neither amount is excludable. Signing bonuses are always taxable, and moving expense reimbursements lost their exclusion under the TCJA.$EXPL$
