-- Q3936: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 56(b)(3), exercising ISOs creates an AMT adjustment equal to the spread between FMV and exercise price: ($35 - $10) x 1,000 = $25,000. This amount is added to alternative minimum taxable income in the exercise year because ISOs receive preferential regular tax treatment.
Wrong (A): ISOs are subject to AMT. While no regular income tax is due at exercise, the spread is an AMT preference item under Sec. 56(b)(3).
Wrong (B): $10,000 incorrectly uses only the exercise price ($10 x 1,000). The AMT adjustment is the spread, not the exercise price alone.
Wrong (D): $35,000 incorrectly uses the full FMV ($35 x 1,000). The adjustment is only the spread between FMV and exercise price.$EXPL$
