Wrong (A): NSO exercises do create employer deductions. Unlike ISOs under Sec. 422, which generally provide no employer deduction, NSOs generate a matching deduction under Sec. 83(h).
Wrong (B): $200,000 incorrectly uses only the exercise price ($20 x 10,000) rather than the spread between FMV and exercise price.
