-- Q3945: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 83(b), the election must be filed with the IRS within 30 days of the date of the property transfer. The election is irrevocable once filed, and it accelerates income recognition to the transfer date rather than the vesting date.
Wrong (A): The 60-day deadline is incorrect. The statutory deadline is 30 days from the property transfer under Sec. 83(b).
Wrong (B): If stock is forfeited after a Sec. 83(b) election, no deduction or loss is allowed for the amount previously included in income.
Wrong (D): The election is irrevocable once filed. It cannot be revoked at any time, even before vesting occurs.$EXPL$
