-- Q3951: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): A same-day sale of ISO shares is a disqualifying disposition under Sec. 422(a)(1) because the one-year holding period from exercise is not met. The spread ($80 - $30) x 500 = $25,000 is ordinary income. No AMT adjustment applies because the shares were disposed of in the same year as exercise.
Wrong (A): The gain cannot be long-term capital gain because the holding period from exercise was zero days, triggering a disqualifying disposition with ordinary income treatment.
Wrong (C): There is a taxable gain. The spread between FMV at exercise and the exercise price ($50 - $30 = $20 per share, not applicable here; actually $80 - $30 = $50 x 500 = $25,000) creates ordinary income on the disqualifying disposition.
Wrong (D): No AMT adjustment applies when ISO shares are disposed of in the same calendar year as exercise. The AMT preference only arises if shares are held past year-end.$EXPL$
