UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 79, employer-provided group-term life insurance coverage is excludable for the first $50,000 of coverage. The cost of coverage exceeding $50,000 is included in the employee''s gross income, calculated using IRS Table I uniform premium rates rather than actual premium costs.
Wrong (A): Not all employer-paid premiums are excludable. The exclusion is limited to the first $50,000 of coverage under Sec. 79.
Wrong (B): Group-term life insurance is not always fully taxable. The first $50,000 of coverage is excludable from the employee''s income.
